# Step 3: before a call runs, its arguments are checked against the tool's
# schema — the executor's job, not the model adapter's: this rule knows
# which definition the call names. The catalogue listed the tools sorted by
# name, so price_quote is `.0` and stock_check is `.1`; a rule per (call,
# tool) keeps the lookup explicit. A call the chassis flagged (`problem`)
# is not checked: it must not run as it is.
WHEN ._turn.tool_calls.0.name == "stock_check" && !exists ._turn.tool_calls.0.problem
  WITH schema = ._tools.tools.1.parameters,
       value  = ._turn.tool_calls.0.arguments,
       into   = "_check0"
  EXEC "txco://schema/check"
